cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ASSAY in your research, please cite it along with the
  frozen protocol revision you used.
title: ASSAY
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: heicfast
    alias: heicfast
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://github.com/heicfast/assay"
repository-code: "https://github.com/heicfast/assay"
abstract: >-
  ASSAY is an open research framework for measuring LLM safety the way
  assays measure purity and strength: a standardized, quantitative test.
  It combines validated multi-judge instrumentation calibrated against
  human labels, a literature-grounded static and adaptive multi-turn
  attack battery, and mechanistic refusal-direction analysis, across the
  frontier model matrix, with preregistered statistics, full provenance,
  fail-closed budgets, and a 90-day coordinated-disclosure pipeline.
keywords:
  - llm-safety
  - red-teaming
  - jailbreak-research
  - measurement-validity
  - interpretability
  - refusal-direction
license: Apache-2.0
